aetherhaven.difficulty.title = Aetherhaven difficulty
aetherhaven.difficulty.easy.title = Easy
aetherhaven.difficulty.easy.desc = Building materials and gold cost half as much.
aetherhaven.difficulty.normal.title = Normal
aetherhaven.difficulty.normal.desc = Standard building costs and town economy.
aetherhaven.difficulty.hard.title = Hard
aetherhaven.difficulty.hard.desc = Buildings and shop buys cost more. Workplace upgrades and item unlocks cost double. Taxes and loot are lower. Selling returns less.
aetherhaven.difficulty.selected = Selected
aetherhaven.difficulty.custom.title = Custom
aetherhaven.difficulty.customize = Customize
aetherhaven.difficulty.back = Back to presets
aetherhaven.difficulty.resourceMult = Building materials cost
aetherhaven.difficulty.resourceMult.tooltip = How many materials it takes to build a town building. Higher means more materials.
aetherhaven.difficulty.goldMult = Building gold cost
aetherhaven.difficulty.goldMult.tooltip = How much treasury gold it costs to build a town building. Higher means more gold.
aetherhaven.difficulty.allBlocks = Require every block in each blueprint
aetherhaven.difficulty.allBlocks.tooltip = When on, you must supply every block used in the building blueprint instead of the usual material list.
aetherhaven.difficulty.buyPriceMult = Shop buy prices
aetherhaven.difficulty.buyPriceMult.tooltip = How expensive items are when buying from shops. Higher means shops charge more.
aetherhaven.difficulty.sellMargin = Shop sell return
aetherhaven.difficulty.sellMargin.tooltip = How much of an item's price you get back when selling at a player shop. Higher means better sell prices.
aetherhaven.difficulty.taxMult = Villager tax income
aetherhaven.difficulty.taxMult.tooltip = How much gold villagers pay into the treasury through taxes. Higher means more tax income.
aetherhaven.difficulty.upgradeGoldMult = Workplace upgrade gold
aetherhaven.difficulty.upgradeGoldMult.tooltip = Gold cost for workplace and restaurant upgrades, like mine or logger upgrades. Higher means upgrades cost more gold.
aetherhaven.difficulty.upgradeResourceMult = Workplace upgrade materials
aetherhaven.difficulty.upgradeResourceMult.tooltip = Material cost for workplace and restaurant upgrades. Higher means upgrades need more materials.
aetherhaven.difficulty.unlockGoldMult = Workplace item unlock gold
aetherhaven.difficulty.unlockGoldMult.tooltip = Gold cost to unlock a new item a workplace can make, like a new ore or wood type. Higher means unlocks cost more gold.
aetherhaven.difficulty.unlockResourceMult = Workplace item unlock materials
aetherhaven.difficulty.unlockResourceMult.tooltip = How many of that item you must turn in to unlock it for production. Higher means unlocks need more materials.
aetherhaven.difficulty.buildingStaffDisabled = Building staff off
aetherhaven.difficulty.buildingStaffDisabled.tooltip = When on, the building staff cannot be used to place or clear building blocks.
aetherhaven.difficulty.goldLootMult = Gold in chests and gifts
aetherhaven.difficulty.goldLootMult.tooltip = How often and how much gold appears in chests and floating gifts. Higher means more gold loot.
aetherhaven.difficulty.otherLootMult = Other Aetherhaven loot
aetherhaven.difficulty.otherLootMult.tooltip = How often jewelry, blueprints, props, and other Aetherhaven loot appear in chests and gifts. Higher means more of that loot.
aetherhaven.difficulty.forceAllTowns = Force all towns to use this
aetherhaven.difficulty.forceAllTowns.tooltip = When on, every town on the server uses these difficulty settings. Town owners cannot pick their own.
aetherhaven.difficulty.serverTitle = Server difficulty
aetherhaven.difficulty.serverForced = The server sets difficulty for every town.
aetherhaven.difficulty.serverLocked = The server sets difficulty. Only an admin can change it.
aetherhaven.difficulty.buildingStaffDisabledMsg = Building staff is turned off for this difficulty.
